@@ -7,12 +7,14 @@ of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
 ## Rental module
 
 `createRentalService()` (exported from `src/index.ts`) returns an in-memory service with
-`addEquipment`, `quote` and `book`. Run the tests with `npm test`.
+`addEquipment`, `quote`, `book` and `availability`. Run the tests with `npm test`.
 
 - Money is an integer number of euro cents; `total` is `dailyPrice` times the number of days.
 - Times are ISO-8601 UTC strings with an explicit `Z`. A period starts and ends at midnight UTC and
   `end` is the start of the day after the last rented day, so `2026-07-01T00:00:00Z` to
   `2026-07-02T00:00:00Z` is one day. Returned times are normalised to `toISOString()` form.
 - An item cannot be booked for overlapping periods; back-to-back periods are fine.
+- `availability({ start, end, kind? })` returns the sorted ids of the items, of that kind or of any kind when
+  none is given, that are free for the whole period (same period rules as `quote`).
 - Invalid input, unknown items and clashing bookings throw an `Error`.
 - Cancellation (no refund under 24 hours before the start, full refund otherwise) is not implemented yet.
